    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds like you're just listing common arguments against it, but you're not actually answering the question if there's a definitive moral framework that *does* justify it. If we look at utilitarianism, wouldn't the math favor a single preemptive strike if it definitively prevents a million deaths later? Why can't you just say under what specific moral conditions it would be right?",
